      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C30", "C31", "C33", "C34", "C35", "C36", "C37", "C40", "C41", "C42", "C43", "C44", "C45", "C46", "C48", "C49", "C50", "C51", "C52", "C53", "C54", "C55", "C58"]
    },
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C32", "C38", "C47", "C56", "C57"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule; transfer relies on structural analogy to lefamulin and BMS-275183 rather than an exact match.",
    "The query is more polar (logD -0.34, TPSA 128.6) and lacks the basic amine of lefamulin, so permeability may be lower; no experimental permeability or first-pass data are available.",
    "No formulation, dose, or species-specific data are available for the query, and oral bioavailability can be formulation-dependent.",
    "Rat tacrolimus low values (C32, C38, C47, C56, C57) highlight species/formulation dependence, but no query-specific data resolve this."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L2 records reinforce the L1 basis: lefamulin F≈25.8% (C05, C24) and BMS-275183 F≈24% (C01, C10, C18) support F≥20% for a complex diterpenoid; low rat tacrolimus values are formulation/species-specific and not transferable. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

